{{- /*
  The Homebrew prefix.

  For configuration files that cannot run a command to find it — Ghostty's
  `command` is a static string, not a shell.

  It is now a constant. Apple Silicon is the only supported platform (ADR-036), so
  /opt/homebrew is the answer whether or not Homebrew is installed yet, and this
  template no longer probes the filesystem. The Intel prefix is deliberately absent:
  on Apple Silicon that path means an x86_64 Homebrew under Rosetta, and emitting it
  here would bake a translated binary's path into a configuration file.

  Kept as a template rather than inlined at the call sites so the prefix still has
  exactly one definition; tests/chezmoi-templates.sh asserts what it renders to.

  The trailing `{{- -}}` below is load-bearing. This template is interpolated INLINE
  — `command = {{ template "brew-prefix" . }}/bin/fish --login` — so an emitted
  trailing newline splits that into two lines and Ghostty receives
  `command = /opt/homebrew`. That is a path which exists, so it fails the way ADR-030
  warns about: quietly, with the wrong shell.
*/ -}}
/opt/homebrew
